1
00:00:03,274 --> 00:00:06,378
Open Settings, Phone Number Verifications.

2
00:00:06,378 --> 00:00:10,710
The General tab holds the rules that apply to every provider.

3
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:15,494
Until a provider is switched on, the page says that none is enabled.

4
00:00:15,991 --> 00:00:18,410
Each service has its own tab.

5
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:22,421
AbstractAPI needs only an API key from your account.

6
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:29,248
Twilio asks for an Authentication type:

7
00:00:29,248 --> 00:00:34,193
an API key SID and secret, which Twilio recommends for everyday use, or

8
00:00:34,193 --> 00:00:37,853
an Account SID and Auth Token, which suits testing.

9
00:00:37,853 --> 00:00:42,541
You can also set a Country code for numbers stored without one, and

10
00:00:42,541 --> 00:00:45,559
Data packages for extra line information.

11
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:57,809
On the Veriphone tab, switch on Enable this provider and paste the API key.

12
00:00:57,809 --> 00:01:02,400
The key is stored securely, and the box stays empty afterward.

13
00:01:04,293 --> 00:01:05,368
Click Save.

14
00:01:05,368 --> 00:01:08,654
The General tab now offers a Default provider.

15
00:01:08,654 --> 00:01:14,593
Choose a provider, or First available provider to use the first one that is switched on.

16
00:01:15,052 --> 00:01:20,088
Revalidation interval says how many days a verified number stays verified.

17
00:01:20,088 --> 00:01:25,061
Maximum verification attempts is how many failed checks in a row the site

18
00:01:25,061 --> 00:01:28,712
accepts before it stops retrying a number by itself.

19
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:34,128
Request delay is the pause between checks when many numbers are checked in a row.

20
00:01:34,128 --> 00:01:37,777
Raise it if the service complains about too many requests.

21
00:01:37,777 --> 00:01:38,747
Click Save.

